userStories.description:
**Goal** — Add the shared thread stream contract, path layout, native-model discovery, nax credentials reader, pinned agent dependency and thread timing constants.

**Motivation** — B1 lets the API create threads and place `THREAD` jobs on a v4 runner, but the runner has nothing that can host one.

**Approach** — Paths (`apps/runner/src/thread/thread-paths.ts`): `threadDirFor(homeDir, threadId)` = `<homeDir>/threads/<threadId>` (`threadId` through `assertSegment`), with `threadWorktreeDir`, `threadTranscriptDir` and `threadMetaPath` for its children `wt`, `transcript` and `thread.json`; `skillCacheDirFor(skillsRoot, sourceId, sha)` = `<skillsRoot>/<sourceId>/<sha>`.

`readNativeModels(naxHome, available: ReadonlySet<string>): Promise<NativeModelSet>` (`apps/runner/src/thread/native-models.ts`), `NativeModelSet = { models: string[]; defaultModel: string | null }`. It reads `<naxHome>/config.json`; a missing, unreadable or non-JSON file, or no `models.native` object, gives `{ models: [], defaultModel: null }`. Each value of `models.native` is a model string or an object with a string `model`. The bare id is the model string with a trailing `[...]` removed; its provider is the text before its first `/`. A tier is kept when its bare id contains a `/`, matches `THREAD_MODEL_ID_RE`, and its provider is in `available`. `models` keeps the tiers' order, without duplicates, at most `THREAD_LIMITS.maxNativeModels`. `defaultModel` is the `balanced` tier's bare id when kept, else `models[0]`, else null. `nativeModelProviders(naxHome): Promise<string[]>` returns the distinct providers of those tiers, sorted, so B3b can ask `nax auth list` for them (a provider with only an ambient credential is listed only when asked for).

`naxCredentialsConfig(naxHome): CredentialsConfig` (`apps/runner/src/thread/nax-credentials.ts`) returns `{ configDir: () => naxHome, readAuthConfig }`; `readAuthConfig` re-reads `<naxHome>/config.json` on every call and returns its `auth` block when it is `{ source: 'file' | 'exec', exec?: { command: string[]; timeoutMs: number }, onChange: 'warn' | 'refuse' }`, else `{ source: 'file', onChange: 'warn' }`.

Protocol additions (`packages/fleet-protocol/src/threads.ts`):
```ts
/** The log stream a THREAD job writes (PUT /fleet/runner/jobs/:jobId/logs/thread). */
export const THREAD_STREAM = 'thread' as const;
export const THREAD_STREAM_LIMITS = { lineMaxBytes: 65_536, streamMaxBytes: 209_715_200 } as const;
/** Same rule as the API's MODEL_ID_RE (apps/api/src/fleet/common/thread-jobs.ts). */
export const THREAD_MODEL_ID_RE = /^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._:\/@-]{0,127}$/;

export type ThreadCloseReason = 'idle' | 'closed' | 'cost_cap' | 'stream_cap' | 'cancelled';
export type ThreadFailReason = 'backend_unavailable' | 'agent_not_logged_in' | 'model_unknown' | 'skill_fetch_failed' | 'worktree_conflict' | 'session_error';

/** Lines the runner writes itself. Every other line of the stream is a nax-agent SessionEvent serialized as JSON. */
export type ThreadRunnerLine =
  | { type: 'session_started'; at: string; resumed: boolean; backend: ThreadBackend; skillShas: string[] }
  | { type: 'session_closed'; at: string; reason: ThreadCloseReason }
  | { type: 'input_consumed'; at: string; messageId: string }
  | { type: 'session_failed'; at: string; reason: ThreadFailReason };
```
Stream contract (for B2): one JSON object per line, UTF-8, `\n`-terminated; a line's size is the byte length of its serialized JSON plus the newline, at most `THREAD_STREAM_LIMITS.lineMaxBytes`. Session lines keep nax-agent's `SessionEvent` fields (`type`, `sessionId`, `turnId`, `at`, `metadata`, body), in the order the session produced them. `text_delta.text`, `thinking_delta.text`, `turn_end.output` and `turn_end.error.message` are redacted as below; `tool_call.input`, `tool_result.preview`, `question.text` and approval summaries carry nax-agent's own best-effort redaction. A `text_delta` too long for one line becomes several `text_delta` lines with the same `turnId` and `round`, in order. A `turn_end` too long for one line is written with `output: ""` and `outputTruncated: true`. Any other session line too long for one line is dropped and reported through the writer's `onWarn`. `stream_reset` lines are written.

**Scope** — In: shared protocol addition, runner-local foundation modules, frozen `TUNING` additions `threadIdleMs: 900_000`, `threadWakeGapMs: 250`, `threadSearchTimeoutMs: 10_000`, `threadSkillFetchTimeoutMs: 120_000`, exact `@nathapp/nax-agent` 0.86.0 pin and bun.lock. Out: repo tools (US-002), skill fetch (US-003), skill tools (US-004), worktree (US-005), session factory (US-006), event writer (US-007); keep `THREAD_LIMITS` and `FLEET_PROTOCOL_VERSION` (3) unchanged. Wiring these blocks into the daemon (protocol v4, `THREAD` ASSIGN parsing, the `threadBackends` capability report, the thread job run, thread commands, Supervisor READOPT and ABANDON for `THREAD` rows, free slots, the heartbeat, `configureCredentials`, registering the `thread` stream with `LogShipper`, running `pruneArchivedThreads` and `pruneSkillCache`) belongs to feature `fleet-s5a-thread-host` (B3b). The API accepting and folding the `thread` stream, and an API parity test pinning `THREAD_MODEL_ID_RE` to the API's `MODEL_ID_RE`, belong to feature `fleet-s5a-thread-ingest` (B2).

**Interface** — `threadDirFor(homeDir, threadId)`, `threadWorktreeDir`, `threadTranscriptDir`, `threadMetaPath`, `skillCacheDirFor(skillsRoot, sourceId, sha)`; `readNativeModels(naxHome, available: ReadonlySet<string>): Promise<NativeModelSet>`; `NativeModelSet = { models: string[]; defaultModel: string | null }`; `nativeModelProviders(naxHome): Promise<string[]>`; `naxCredentialsConfig(naxHome): CredentialsConfig`.

Build gate: also run `bun run type-check` at the repo root (this story edits packages/fleet-protocol/src/threads.ts).
